body:
**Simplify, and one I'd take alongside the fixes because this round created the third copy.**

"A block proved it exists, so every open absence below it is interior memory, the run closes, and this block is the new top" is the single most load-bearing rule in the sweep, and it's written three times -- here, at `:760-763`, and at `:839-842` with the `+ 1` folded in. It is stated as one thing nowhere.

```c
// A block just proved it exists. Every absence still open below it is therefore interior memory that
// answered nothing -- a fault, not the space above the card -- so count those (their bits are already
// set) and close the run. This block becomes the top the report is measured against.
static void iso15693_poller_wipe_note_present(
    Iso15693Poller* instance, uint16_t block,
    uint16_t* absent_run, bool* any_present, uint16_t* highest_present);
```

Sites 1 and 2 become one call. Site 3 becomes the call plus `clone_failed_count++` -- arithmetically identical to `+= still_absent + 1`, and it lets you drop `still_absent` and reuse `absent_run` directly (set it to 0 before the probe loop, increment where `still_absent++` was, delete the trailing assignment). Same value at every observation point, one fewer name for the same quantity.

Use `if(block > *highest_present)` in the helper: it preserves site 3's guard rather than dropping it, and sites 1/2 are unaffected because `block` ascends there.

**Simplify, and the second one I'd take now, because the drift this comment promises to prevent has already happened.**

The button gate in `on_enter` is `over_capacity || (failed_count > 0 && wipe_uid_changed) || (partial && (failed_count > 0 || used_gen1 || identity_failed))`. The routing here is `partial || over_capacity || wipe_uid_changed`. They disagree for `wipe_uid_changed && failed_count == 0`: the routing accepts it, the gate rejects it. Harmless only because no right-hand button is drawn on that path -- so it's latent, not live.

One predicate used by both:

```c
static bool nfc_magic_scene_iso15693_write_fail_has_details(NfcMagicApp* instance, uint32_t reason) {
    const Iso15693PollerResult* r = &instance->iso15693_result;
    switch(reason) {
    case NfcMagicIso15693WriteFailReasonOverCapacity:   return true;
    case NfcMagicIso15693WriteFailReasonPartial:        return r->failed_count > 0 || r->used_gen1 || r->identity_failed;
    case NfcMagicIso15693WriteFailReasonWipeUidChanged: return r->failed_count > 0;
    default:                                            return false;
    }
}
```

`on_event` then keeps only `card_lost`. Precedent for a file-local scene helper is `nfc_magic_scene_write.c:213`. It survives the queued `{reason, title, body}` table untouched -- that replaces the render chain, not this gate -- and it's where `sweep_truncated` wants to go for the Partial and UID-changed findings.

The eleven `const bool`s at `:20-31` I'd leave alone: the table deletes them all, and a partial cleanup just conflicts with it.

**Simplify, minor.** `protocol == Iso15693` is tested at `:381` and again here; `iso15693_mode == Wipe` at `:397` and again at `:402`. Two locals at the top of the branch make the gate and the reason read off the same fact instead of each re-deriving it:

```c
const bool iso15693 = (instance->protocol == NfcMagicProtocolIso15693);
const bool iso15693_wipe = iso15693 && (instance->iso15693_mode == NfcMagicIso15693ModeWipe);
```

Don't reuse `nfc_magic_scene_write_is_wiping()` here -- it also returns true for `uscuid_ul_is_wipe_mode`, which would be wrong in this branch.
